  Result = String of 64 lowercase hex digits.
MECHANISM SHA-256 (R1) is implemented in the crate per FIPS 180-4 (the standard initial hash values and 64 round
  constants, big-endian words, the 0x80 / zero / 64-bit bit-length padding) over P.as_bytes(); hex = format!("{:02x}").
MECHANISM WS membership = a match on exactly the 25 code points of the primary's WS pin; leading/trailing WS removal =
  trim_matches / trim_end_matches with that predicate. NOT char::is_whitespace, str::trim or str::split_whitespace
  (they use Unicode White_Space: 0085 in, FEFF out). LT = a match on the 4 code points of the LT pin.
MECHANISM splitting (R2) = str::split('\n') (yields the empty final piece, as js), then strip_suffix('\r') once. The
  scanners of R5, R6 and R8 are hand-written over a Vec<char>; INDENT (R3) is the prefix of ' ' and '\t' only.
MECHANISM ATTRS (R10) = a Vec<(&'static str, String)> kept in first-store order: storing an existing key replaces its
  value in place (R9) or, inside one R8 run, appends " " + value only when the old value is non-empty.
